    "text_full": "Skip to content\nAbout Us\nPrograms\nNews & Media\nDONATE\nFR\nHERITAGE MINUTES\nPODCASTS\nVIDEOS\nEDUCATION GUIDES\nSEARCH PRODUCTIONS\nHome\n / Videos / Citizenship Challenge\nCitizenship Challenge\n\nThe Citizenship Challenge asks Canadians to test their national knowledge by studying for and writing a mock citizenship exam in French or English, and also creates learning tools and videos to increase our understanding of topics related to citizenship and history.\n\nFeatures\nThe Vikings\nNew!\nNorse Sagas and archaeological findings at L’Anse aux Meadows in Newfoundland come together to reveal the history of the first European presence in Canada.\nAll (7) Episodes\nSort by:\nDate\nA to Z\nSearch & Filter\nThe Vikings\n2025\nProhibition and the Yukon\n2024\nBreaking Chains: Thornton and Lucie Blackburn's Journey from Enslavement to Freedom\n2023\nWomen's Rights Leader Thérèse Casgrain\n2020\nSamuel de Champlain and the Founding of Quebec City\n2020\nAfricville: The Black community bulldozed by the city of Halifax\n2020\nOperation Soap: The police raids that targeted Toronto’s queer community in the 1980s\n2020\n\nHistorica Canada is a charitable organization that offers programs in both official languages that you can use to explore, learn, reflect on our history, and consider what it means to be Canadian.\n\nHistorica Canada's business number is 885434720RR0001\n\nAbout Us\nPolicies\nCareers\nHistorica Canada Content Usage Request Form\n\nFollow Us\nMore From Historica Canada\nCitizenship Challenge\nHeritage Minutes\nThe Memory Project\nThe Canadian Encyclopedia\nPartnership: The World Remembers\n© Historica Canada 2026. All rights reserved.\nWebsite by DS"
